        {
            "label": "Google Fonts / custom font fields",
            "group": "Fonts",
            "type": "separator",
            "note": "Only used when Font source is Google Fonts or Custom. To use Google Fonts: <br>1. Go to <a href='https://fonts.google.com' target='_blank'>fonts.google.com</a> and select your styles.<br>2. In the 'Embed Code' section, look for the <code>family=</code> part of the URL.<br>3. Copy the part after the equals sign into the <b>URL Segment</b> field (e.g., <code>Libre+Baskerville:wght@700</code>).<br>4. Enter the simple name in the <b>Family Name</b> field (e.g., <code>Libre Baskerville</code>)."
        },
